# 🕹️ Godot 4 Hierarchical State Machine (HSM) Architecture

This skill provides a robust, decoupled, and typed **Hierarchical Finite State Machine** system for Godot 4.x entities.

---

## 🏗️ 1. Hierarchical State Architecture

Instead of a giant flat FSM where every state knows every other state, use a nested hierarchy with clean delegation.

```mermaid
stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> Grounded
    
    state Grounded {
        [*] --> Idle
        Idle --> Running : move input > 0
        Running --> Idle : move input == 0
    }
    
    Grounded --> InAir : jump / fall
    
    state InAir {
        [*] --> Jumping
        Jumping --> Falling : velocity.y >= 0
    }
    
    InAir --> Grounded : is_on_floor()
    Grounded --> Attacking : attack pressed
    Attacking --> Grounded : animation finished
```

---

## 💎 2. Core State Base Class (`State.gd`)

```gdscript
# res://src/core/components/state_machine/state.gd
class_name State
extends Node

## Base State class for Godot 4 Hierarchical State Machines.
## All individual state nodes inherit from this class.

signal transitioned(next_state_name: StringName, payload: Dictionary)

## Reference to the root actor (e.g., CharacterBody2D / CharacterBody3D).
var actor: Node = null

## Reference to the parent StateMachine.
var state_machine: StateMachine = null

## Called once when the State Machine initializes.
func initialize(p_actor: Node, p_machine: StateMachine) -> void:
	actor = p_actor
	state_machine = p_machine

## Called when entering this state.
func enter(_payload: Dictionary = {}) -> void:
	pass

## Called when exiting this state.
func exit() -> void:
	pass

## Called every frame from _process().
func update(_delta: float) -> void:
	pass

## Called every physics frame from _physics_process().
func physics_update(_delta: float) -> void:
	pass

## Called during unhandled input events.
func handle_input(_event: InputEvent) -> void:
	pass
```

